<title>USA: John Wiley Q3 shr $0.41, after $0.08 loss.</title>
<headline>John Wiley Q3 shr $0.41, after $0.08 loss.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>JOHN WILEY &amp; SONS, INC.</p>
<p>			     SUMMARY OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>	   FOR THE THIRD QUARTER AND NINE MONTHS</p>
<p>		 ENDED JANUARY 31, 1997 AND 1996</p>
<p>		     Third Quarter	     Nine Months</p>
<p>		   Ended January 31,	 Ended January 31,</p>
<p>			 1997	 1996	   1997	   1996</p>
<p>Revenues  $118,105,000  97,409,000  324,392,000  272,332,000 Operating Income</p>
<p>		 11,913,000  10,710,000   30,818,000   29,325,000</p>
<p>Income Before Taxes</p>
<p>		 10,526,000  15,421,000   27,281,000   34,351,000</p>
<p> Net Income   6,731,000   9,835,000   17,454,000   21,193,000</p>
<p>Net Income Per Share</p>
<p>  Primary	    0.41	  0.59	   1.06	   1.28</p>
<p>  Fully Diluted    0.41	  0.59	   1.06	   1.28</p>
<p>Average Shares</p>
<p>  Primary    16,294,000  16,604,000   16,430,000   16,542,000</p>
<p>Fully Diluted</p>
<p>		 16,340,000  16,616,000   16,450,000   16,576,000</p>
<p>NOTE: 1997 Q3 net income includes a charge of $1.3 million or $0.08 a share, relating to the amortization of intangibles and financing costs associated with the acquisition of VCH Publishing Group.</p>
<p>1996 Q3 net income includes a special item of $2.6 million or $0.16 per share, relating to interest received on the favorable resolution of amended tax return claims.</p>
